[106.571, "o", "## Schema Design (BigQuery)\r\n\r\n**Partitioning & clustering recommendations:**\r\n- **Partition by `DATE`** on the actual `order_date` column (not ingestion time), so queries filter directly on business date.\r\n- For 50M rows, prefer **MONTHLY partitioning** (~1.7M rows/partition) if queries usually span a month+, or **daily** if users query single-day windows frequently. Limits: 4,000 partitions/table, so daily \u2248 11 years.\r\n- **Cluster by** `customer_id` (high-cardinality, commonly filtered) and `order_status` (low-cardinality, hot in WHERE clauses). Max 4 clustering cols \u2014 order them by cardinality desc: `customer_id, order_status, ship_country`.\r\n\r\n**DDL:**\r\n\r\n```sql\r\nCREATE OR REPLACE TABLE `my_dataset.orders`\r\nPARTITION BY order_date                          -- DATE column, NOT ingestion-time\r\nCLUSTER BY customer_id, order_status, ship_country\r\nOPTIONS (\r\n  partition_expiration_days = 1095,               -- retain 3 yrs of history\r\n  description = \"E-commerce orders, 50M rows\"\r\n) AS ...\r\n\r\n-- Schema\r\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS `my_dataset.orders` (\r\n  order_id        STRING NOT NULL,                -- use STRING for opaque IDs\r\n  customer_id     STRING NOT NULL,\r\n  order_date      DATE NOT NULL,                  -- partitioning column\r\n  order_status    STRING NOT NULL,                -- e.g. PENDING/SHIPPED/CANCELLED\r\n  payment_method  STRING,\r\n  item_count      INT64,\r\n  total_amount    NUMERIC(19,4),                  -- NUMERIC, never FLOAT, for money\r\n  discount_amount BIGNUMERIC,                     -- if needed beyond 38 digits\r\n  ship_country    STRING,\r\n  tags            ARRAY<STRING>,                  -- promote repeating attrs to REPEATED\r\n  meta            JSON,                           -- JSON for sparse/flexible fields\r\n  last_updated    TIMESTAMP\r\n)\r\nPARTITION BY order_date\r\nCLUSTER BY customer_id, order_status, ship_country;\r\n\r\n-- Index-armed via cluster metadata; optional secondary table keyed by customer_id\r\nCREATE TABLE `my_dataset.orders_by_customer`\r\nPARTITION BY DATE_TRUNC(order_date, MONTH)\r\nCLUSTER BY customer_id;\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Rationale at 50M rows:**\r\n- Serverless scan-based pricing \u2192 pruning beats indexes: partition + cluster cuts scanned bytes for `WHERE order_date BETWEEN ... AND customer_id = X AND order_status = 'SHIPPED'` to a tiny slice.\r\n- `NUMERIC/BIGNUMERIC` for money avoids float rounding.\r\n- Use `JSON` type instead of many nullable columns for sparse metadata; keep high-query-rate fields as first-class columns.\r\n- Optionally create a federated/duplicate table tuned per access pattern (`orders_by_customer`) since BigQuery charges per query, not for storage duplication.\r\n\r\nWould you like the corresponding `bq mk` CLI or Terraform (see `references/iac-usage.md`) version?\r\n"]
